2. DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

2.1 "Model" means the Berna Prototype 162M, including model weights,
    trained parameters, model configuration, tokenizer files, model
    code, inference-related code, checkpoints, associated metadata,
    and files expressly identified by the Original Creator as part
    of the Model distribution.

2.2 "Original Model" means the Model as distributed by the Original
    Creator, without modification to its weights.

2.3 "Derivative Model" means a model whose weights or trained
    parameters are materially derived from the Model through
    fine-tuning, continued training, retraining, parameter
    adaptation, weight transformation, merging, distillation,
    pruning, or another process that materially incorporates or
    derives trained parameters from the Model.

2.4 "Non-Commercial Use" means use undertaken without the primary
    purpose or effect of obtaining monetary compensation, commercial
    advantage, or revenue. Examples: personal experimentation,
    academic research, teaching, education, nonprofit research,
    evaluation, benchmarking, and private development.

2.5 "Commercial Use" means any use primarily intended for, or
    resulting in: direct or indirect revenue, commercial advantage,
    monetized services, paid products, paid APIs, paid inference,
    commercial deployment, commercial integration, sale, licensing,
    rental, leasing, or use within a commercial product or service.

2.6 "Distribution" means making the Model or a copy of the Model
    available to another person or entity.

2.7 "Creator" or "Original Creator" or "Licensor" means:
    Muhamed Kamil

