4. NON-COMMERCIAL MODIFICATION AND EXPERIMENTATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------

The Creator permits modification of a local copy of the Model solely
for Non-Commercial Use, subject to the following conditions.

4.1 Permitted Local Research
    You may, for Non-Commercial Use only:
    - fine-tune the Model;
    - continue-train the Model;
    - perform experimental retraining;
    - quantize the Model;
    - prune the Model;
    - modify inference configurations;
    - conduct model-merging experiments;
    - perform experimental distillation;
    - and otherwise modify the Model for research.

4.2 No Redistribution of Modified Models
    A modified or Derivative Model may not be distributed, published,
    uploaded, sold, licensed, rented, leased, or otherwise made
    available to third parties under this license.

    This restriction applies regardless of whether the modified
    Model is fine-tuned, quantized, pruned, merged, distilled,
    compressed, converted, or otherwise transformed.

4.2.1 Limited Academic Research Exception
    Notwithstanding Section 4.2, an accredited academic institution,
    nonprofit research organization, or individual academic
    researcher may distribute a Derivative Model for strictly
    non-commercial academic research purposes, subject to all of the
    following conditions:
    (a) the distribution is made through an academic channel (e.g.,
        a university repository, an academic preprint server, or a
        peer-reviewed publication's supplementary materials);
    (b) no fee, subscription, or commercial consideration is charged
        for access to the Derivative Model;
    (c) full attribution to the Original Creator is given as
        specified in Section 6;
    (d) this license is included in full with the distributed
        Derivative Model;
    (e) the Derivative Model is clearly identified as a modified
        version, and is not represented as the Original Model;
    (f) the academic institution or researcher provides the Original
        Creator with reasonable advance written notice via the
        contact channel specified in Section 20; and
    (g) the Derivative Model is not used, directly or indirectly,
        for any Commercial Use under Section 2.5.

    The Original Creator reserves the right to revoke this academic
    exception for any specific distribution upon reasonable written
    notice if the Creator determines that the distribution
    materially harms the integrity, security, or commercial
    interests of the Berna project.

4.3 Research Artifacts
    Research results such as papers, benchmark results, evaluations,
    measurements, analyses, screenshots, charts, and textual
    descriptions may be published provided that such publication
    does not distribute the Model or a Derivative Model in violation
    of this license.

